@startuml
title Phase 2 target architecture (step 2 design, not current runtime)
package "Host / composition (steps 3-4)" as Host {
  [Code assembly A] as A
  [Config module loader B] as B
  [Filesystem adapters] as IO
}
package "Core" {
  [public contracts] as Public
  [PluginRegistry] as Registry
  [Session / document / history\n(step 3 migration)] as Runtime
  [Generic presentation / SVG\n(step 3 migration)] as Render
  [AttributeDispatcher / TreeLabels] as Hooks
}
package "Plugins (steps 3, 5-7)" as Plugins {
  [Default commands / six providers] as Builtin
  [stats / dir / box / modified-star] as Optional
}
A --> Registry : activate(manifest, instance, options)
B --> Registry : same activation path
A --> Plugins : construct
B --> Plugins : resolve module strings
IO ..|> Public : implement ports
Registry --> Public
Runtime --> Public
Render --> Public
Hooks --> Public
Runtime --> Hooks
Render --> Hooks
Builtin --> Public
Optional --> Public
Host --> Runtime : wire dependencies
note bottom of Public
  Four extension points and public domain/session/IO protocols.
  No dependency on plugin implementations or the host.
end note
@enduml
